  "question": {
    "text": "The Spin only magnetic moment value of square planar complex <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Pt</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mi>Cl</mi></math> is _______ B.M. (Nearest integer)<br/>( Given atomic number for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Pt</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>78</mn><mo>)</mo></math>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "0",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Spin only magnetic moment can be calculated by the following formula<br/>Magnetic moment =<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt></math><br/>Where, n is number of unpaired electrons.</p><p>In the given compound, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Pt</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>8</mn></msup></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0095_f7af4c3e3e8e.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 364px;\"/></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Pt</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>→</mo><msup><mi>dsp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> hybridization and have no unpaired electrons..</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo></math> Magnetic moment</p><p> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>0</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>"
  }
}